Leave activators, doors and containers out of active grid object paging chunks (cell change hitch fix).

With "object paging active grid" on, the terrain preload builds the paging chunks for the next grid in
the background before the player crosses into it. But activators, doors and containers are animated:
when their cell is loaded, Scene::addObject hands them to the mechanics, World::getAnimation finds
them paged, takes them out of paging and blacklists them, and the blacklist drops every active grid
chunk around them. So the chunks the preload had just built for the new cells were thrown away and
built again on the main thread (the focus ray or the cull reach them first), each time a cell was
entered for the first time in a session. Measured on a Retroid Pocket Duo Lite with the DSPerf probe
and simpleperf: about 140 ms of a 260 ms frame on a west step, all of it ObjectPaging::createChunk.

These three types never stay in an active grid chunk, so they are now left out of those chunks from
the start, and blacklisting one of them no longer drops chunks. Distant chunks keep them as before.

